From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:04:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Restore Bluetooth and WWAN state on resume

_PTS turns the radios off through RADI(0), and on S3 resume ramstage
turns Bluetooth and WWAN back on according to the "bluetooth" and
"wwan" options, both enabled by default. The state that thinkpad_acpi
asked to restore at resume (SBDC/SWAN) is never applied, because _WAK
does not call HKEY.WAKE like the other boards with an H8 EC do. A radio
turned off by the user comes back on after every suspend.

Call HKEY.WAKE from _WAK.

TEST=Built for W541 and T440p. Not tested on hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
index 42587fd78..07381b80e 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 
 Method(_WAK,1)
 {
+	/* Wake the HKEY to init BT/WWAN */
+	\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WAKE (Arg0)
+
 	Return(Package(){0,0})
 }
 
